       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I need you to confirm the dose first.\n\n**The problem:** Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the maximum recommended dose. For adults the usual range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg is the most you'd normally give. A 50 mg dose could cause severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, or a shock picture. Amlodipine overdoses can also last a long time because the drug has a long half-life.\n\nThe order looks like it might be a typo, for example 5 mg (a common starting dose) with an extra zero.\n\n**Can you tell me which you meant?**\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily** (or another dose between 2.5 and 10 mg). I'll enter it right away.\n2. **Amlodipine 50 mg PO once daily, on purpose.** If so, please give me the clinical reason so I can add it as a note on the order, and expect pharmacy to check it too."
      }
