       "text": "I'm still not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily. I know you're the prescriber and this is your decision. But this dose is 5 times the maximum, there's no recognized reason to give it, and a mistake here could seriously harm the patient. Your confirmation alone isn't enough for me to submit it.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- **Enter a dose within the normal range.** For example, 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily. Just tell me the dose and I'll submit it right away.\n- **Enter 50 mg if you give me a clinical reason.** If there's something specific to this patient, such as a protocol or a specialist's recommendation, tell me and I'll put it in the order note so pharmacy can see it.\n- **Use your usual override process.** If you're sure about 50 mg and don't want to explain it here, you can enter it yourself through the CPOE dose-override process. That way it's recorded under your name and pharmacy will review it.\n\nWhich would you like?"
